body:
My solution
- fixed pattern to create links with subdomain with underscore and domain without underscore;
- works with: ftp://user:pass@host.com and ftp://host.com;
- using DomDocument and DomXPath;

  ```
  $pattern = '@((ftps?\://)(([a-z0-9-_]+(\:?[^\s])*)\@)?|(https?\://)(www\.)?)([a-z0-9]([a-z0-9_]|(\-[a-z0-9]))*\.)?([a-z0-9]([a-z0-9]|(\-[a-z0-9]))*\.)+([a-zA-Z]{2,})(\/([^\s<)])*)*@i';

  $doc = new DOMDocument();
  $doc->loadHTML('<?xml encoding="UTF-8">' . $text);

  $path = new DOMXPath($doc);

  foreach ($path->query('//text()[not(ancestor::a)]') as $node) {
      if (preg_match($pattern, $node->textContent)) {
          $node->nodeValue = preg_replace($pattern, '<a href="$0">$0</a>', $node->nodeValue);
      }
  }

  return htmlspecialchars_decode($doc->getElementsByTagName('p')->item(0)->nodeValue);
  ```

We can add more tags to omitag (like `area` or `link`).

The disadvantage is, we must set encoding (read from bootrstrap?)... but maybe is other solution.
